For review-count states $s\sim\mu$, conditional rating laws $
u_s$, review count $N(s)$, and posterior rating $X_s$, assume $\mathbb E_{
u_s}[X_s]$ equals the fixed-model posterior mean and $\mathbb E_{
u_s}[(X_s-\mathbb E_{
u_s}X_s)^2]$ equals the fixed-model variance for every $s$. Then $\mathbb E_s\mathbb E_{
u_s}[(X_s-q_v)^2]=\mathbb E_s[\operatorname{Bias}(N(s))^2]+\mathbb E_s[\operatorname{Var}(N(s))]$.
